This patch fixes the unbearable slowness of the Windows tty port. If you
are happy with the speed of the official windows binary, then you don't
need it.

I got further with this than I thought I would. There are still some bugs,
all of them glaring and annoying. Immediately obvious are: the cursor
positioning is still mostly (but not completely) wrong, and More/(end)
menu prompts are rainbow cloured. If anybody wants to have a go at fixing
them, then please do so. I don't think I will be able to do much else with
this unless I spend a huge amount of time learning the architecture of the
NetHack source code.

Also, it seems that not everybody experiences the slowdown that this patch
fixes. If you don't, but still want to work on this patch, all you have to
remember is one thing: don't update the cursor position after every output
event. That's what causes the problem in the first place.

Michael

